        <item>
            <title>1.5.14</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 18:36:16 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>46</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5.14</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Inline rename could rename the wrong file.</b> In Details/List view, if the listing re-sorted while the name editor was open — which reliably happened right after New Text Document / New Folder, because creating the item also bumps the folder's `.DS_Store` timestamp — the commit resolved its target by row index and renamed whatever slid into that row (typically `.DS_Store`). Symptoms included a spurious "name is already taken" alert after creating a new text document, and renamed "text" files that TextEdit refused to open (they contained `.DS_Store` binary data). The rename now always targets the item the editor was opened on. Icon views were unaffected.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
